# Cloudflare Pages redirects and rewrites (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
# First match wins. A 200 is a rewrite: the address bar keeps the URL, the page at the target is served.
#
# Night Shift (the member-facing name of the Fun Factory; internal names stay factory): the pages moved from
# /factory to /shift. Every old /factory address redirects for good, keeping the rest of the path.
/factory    /shift    301
/factory/    /shift/    301
/factory/*    /shift/:splat    301

# Club Pass (docs/specs/club-pass.md §3): the old placeholder /club and the How it works address both land on the one page.
/club    /club-pass    301
/club/    /club-pass    301
/club-pass/how-it-works    /club-pass    301
/club-pass/how-it-works/    /club-pass    301

# Creator Climb (docs/specs/creator-climb.md §15): the old Squarespace growth pages.
/growth-2025    /climb    301
/growth-2025/    /climb    301
/growth-2026    /climb    301
/growth-2026/    /climb    301

# Game Vault (docs/specs/game-vault.md §9): every /games/{slug} is the one client-rendered game page
# (/games/view/, which reads the slug from the address). The queue and How it works pages are real
# pages, so they are matched first and rewritten to themselves; without those lines they would
# load as games.
/games/queue    /games/queue/  200
/games/queue/   /games/queue/  200
/games/how-it-works    /games/how-it-works/  200
/games/how-it-works/   /games/how-it-works/  200
/games/:slug    /games/view/   200
/games/:slug/   /games/view/   200

# Member profiles (docs/specs/rewards.md §11): every /u/{handle} is the one client-rendered profile
# page (/u/view/, which reads the handle from the address).
/u/:handle      /u/view/       200
/u/:handle/     /u/view/       200

# Referral links (docs/specs/mod-machina.md §9): every /join/@handle is the one client-rendered page
# (/join/view/), which keeps the handle for 30 days and opens the Join free dialog.
/join/:handle   /join/view/    200
/join/:handle/  /join/view/    200
